# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL. The stack runs with built-in defaults and no .env
# file at all (`docker compose up` just works). Copy this to `.env` only to
# override credentials, change publish settings, or enable a TLS profile.
# Matrix accounts are added at runtime (POST /v1/accounts/login or /import),
# not via this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: store_key is NOT set here. `axon init` generates it once, on first boot,
# onto the axon-data volume (/var/lib/axon/axon.toml). Deleting/replacing that
# volume or config regenerates the key and ORPHANS all encrypted data (account
# tokens + historical Megolm keys) — back the volume up, do not reset it lightly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Postgres (used to build DATABASE_URL for axon-server) ---
# Postgres is bridge-internal (not published to the host), so the default password
# is a formality between two containers. Uncomment/change only if you publish 5432.
#POSTGRES_USER=axon
#POSTGRES_PASSWORD=axon
#POSTGRES_DB=axon

# --- HTTP front door (the `web` service: SPA + proxied API) ---
# These govern the single published :8080 that serves the browser client AND the
# API (/v1, /healthz, /v1/ws) — axon-server itself is not published. Open the
# browser at http://<host>:AXON_PORT, and point the TUI at the same URL. Default
# bind 0.0.0.0 exposes it to the LAN. When running a TLS profile (tailscale/caddy),
# set 127.0.0.1 so only the proxy is reachable from outside the host.
#AXON_PUBLISH_ADDR=0.0.0.0
#AXON_PORT=8080

# --- First web sign-in (zero-paste bootstrap) ---
# By default the stack arms the one-time first-credential web bootstrap: on first
# boot the server prints a URL (http://<host>:PORT/bootstrap/<code>) whose setup
# page mints your first credential and signs the web client in with nothing to
# copy. The code is unguessable and works once. `run-docker.sh` surfaces this URL.
# Set to false to skip the bootstrap and use token-paste instead (then mint a
# token with `docker compose exec axon-server axon token issue`).
#AXON_BOOTSTRAP_WEB=true

# When the bootstrap is DISABLED (AXON_BOOTSTRAP_WEB=false): on first boot the
# container instead mints and prints a client bearer token to the logs (it prints
# ONCE). Set this to false to suppress it and mint out-of-band instead —
# recommended if you ship these logs to an aggregator. (Ignored while the web
# bootstrap is armed, since no token is minted at init then.)
#AXON_INIT_PRINT_TOKEN=false

# --- Optional: run prebuilt images instead of building from source ---
# By default the stack builds axon-server and the web client from this checkout.
# Beta testers can point these at a published image (see deploy/README.md) and
# `docker compose pull` instead. Requires `docker login ghcr.io` (read:packages).
#AXON_SERVER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/matrix-axon/axon-server:beta
#AXON_WEB_IMAGE=ghcr.io/matrix-axon/axon-web:beta

# Accounts are added at runtime, not provisioned on boot: POST
# /v1/accounts/login (password) or POST /v1/accounts/import (an existing
# access_token + device_id) — see the API docs.

# --- Optional: caddy profile (public domain + Let's Encrypt) ---
#DOMAIN=axon.example.org
#ACME_EMAIL=you@example.org

# --- Optional: tailscale profile (remote access over your tailnet) ---
# Generate an auth key at https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys
#TS_AUTHKEY=tskey-auth-xxxxxxxxxxxx
#TS_HOSTNAME=axon
